{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779034317,"nonce":"qbgr7U0WayukpfP3vjmmdzV/TE4=","title":"Chat shell polish: compact rail, grouped sidebar, and composer fixes","message":"## Problem\nThe unified conversation workspace is directionally correct, but the current UI still carries artifacts from the old live/history split and from implementation scaffolding:\n- The app rail is too wide because it shows text labels and the full Mandible wordmark.\n- The conversation sidebar is a flat, noisy list instead of a Codex-style set of foldable sections for pinned items, projects, and loose chats.\n- Branch/model/source metadata is repeated in the sidebar/header where it adds visual bulk rather than actionable context.\n- Composer controls are not consistently usable: Codex history entries are not editable, Claude text can be entered but not reliably submitted, the send affordance is text-heavy, and the model selector is not presented like a first-class dropdown.\n- Chat titles can render Markdown-like formatting or oversized text.\n- Subagent sessions currently appear as their own top-level project, which misrepresents the parent/child relationship.\n\n## Scope\nImplement a high-scrutiny polish pass that:\n- Defaults the top-level app rail to icon-only navigation with hover names and a compact M mark.\n- Adds a hide/reveal shelf affordance for the conversation sidebar, with shared-sidebar generalization tracked separately.\n- Organizes conversations into foldable Pinned, Projects, and Chats sections; supports hover actions for pinning and renaming.\n- Removes branch/meta clutter from chat list items and the conversation header.\n- Strips Markdown formatting from displayed conversation titles.\n- Hides subagent conversations from the top-level chat list for now, pending nested parent display.\n- Makes the composer focusable, sends with Enter and Cmd/Ctrl+Enter, supports Shift+Enter newline, uses an icon send button, removes the stale 'history' label, and exposes model choice as a dropdown where the backend supports updating it.\n- Adds a conservative UI-only fallback for encoded Claude project path names while central project registry work remains tracked separately.\n\n## Out of scope\n- Full central project registry / repo mapping refactor.\n- Native desktop right-click menus and placement of the shelf icon beside macOS window controls.\n- Drag-reordering projects.\n- Full nested subagent display under parent conversations.\n- Backend support for changing the future resume model when no live/resumable transport accepts that setting yet.\n\n## Verification\n- Build the TypeScript/UI bundle in the feature worktree without committing dist.\n- Smoke-test the chat route in the in-app browser, including sidebar structure, hide/reveal, title rendering, composer focus, and submit affordances.\n- Inspect the duplicated `look at issue fa3978f` Codex conversations enough to distinguish real forks/sessions from accidental duplicates.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}